  "limitations": [
    "Caller-serialized Step/Pending/NextWake driver; no new worker/timer. Explicit seeds only. Local demand epoch is not a Redis configuration epoch. A stale-at-publication map cannot clear newer demand.",
    "Close releases coordinator references and publishes immutable outcomes; pending native FIFO duties/resources remain independent. The owner closes Nodes and joins its engine. Observer cancellation never cancels the shared cohort.",
    "Control cap covers coordinator/seeds/two workboxes; per-map cap includes topology/retained Reply reservation. Future/native wire/parser limits remain independently bounded. Caller-retained old maps/outcomes are caller-owned storage.",
    "Performance compares single-caller warm Snapshot acquisition with a lower-bound direct reference control of the identical map. They have different semantics; no equivalent-feature speedup claim. Per-call clock/gate/ref/validation costs remain. No zero-overhead or lock-free claim.",
    "Unpinned serial local microbenchmarks and WSL are not concurrent/fixed-arrival/mixed-load/native Linux/upstream/CPU/RSS/72h production acceptance. Clock floors and noise qualification are recorded before any tail conclusion.",
    "Real metadata queries use prewarmed verified owned plaintext IPv4/default-user Redis 8 pools. Cold bootstrap is fixture-tested; full real TLS/auth/trust and server-topology changes are not validated here.",
    "Automatic MOVED invalidation wiring, refreshed seed selection, replica policy, fully managed asynchronous facade and full four-library production acceptance remain open."
  ],
